# Initiative portrait sets

The six PNG files beside this README are stable runtime aliases. They currently contain the
promoted `matched-bust-v2` set. The truthful former live-figure crops under `v1/` are the permanent
recovery path used if a production alias fails to load.

## Matched bust v2 intake

Production replacement art may arrive as one three-up Fighter/Zombie/Skeleton sheet or as three
separate sources. Every art-directed crop must be square and at least 384 × 384 source pixels. The
spec records an exact source hash, crop, hand-placed eye Y, alpha/matte policy, and provenance for
each identity. Use [`v2-source.example.json`](v2-source.example.json) as the editable schema.
An art-directed square may extend beyond the source canvas; that region becomes transparent
padding, is recorded in the receipt, and is allowed only when at least 384 governed source pixels
remain on both axes.

The default alpha path expects transparent-background PNG source art. An opaque, truly flat source
may instead declare an explicit color matte:

```json
"matte": { "mode": "color", "rgb": [12, 12, 13], "threshold": 18, "softness": 20 }
```

Do not use color-matte removal on a textured or graduated background; regenerate or isolate the
source first. The validator rejects a source crop below 384 px, a hash mismatch, an eye outside the
shared normalized band, a silhouette outside 70–85% vertical occupancy, any silhouette touching
the outer 1% safe edge, an incomplete identity set, or missing provenance. Occupancy means the
visible silhouette's top-to-bottom extent divided by the square crop height—not opaque pixel area.

Build a candidate without changing production aliases:

```sh
python3 tools/build-initiative-portraits.py build-v2 path/to/edited-spec.json
```

This writes `v2/` transactionally only after all three identities pass. Inspect that complete set
at 56 CSS px and DPR2, then promote it:

```sh
python3 tools/build-initiative-portraits.py contact-sheet path/to/contact-sheet.png
python3 tools/build-initiative-portraits.py promote-v2
```

Promotion rechecks source and output hashes before replacing the six stable aliases and their
manifest. It never alters `v1/`. The runtime retries the versioned v1 pair once if a stable alias
cannot load. Unknown figure IDs continue to use the existing letter fallback.

Reproduce the pipeline's acceptance and failure cases with:

```sh
python3 tools/build-initiative-portraits.py self-test
```

The production manifest is the receipt. Generated source art still requires the founder's visual
approval; passing geometry and hash checks cannot approve identity, lighting, armor, or expression.
